Modify SCF file Base On Package Version
    [Arguments]  ${ne_type}  ${swversion}  ${pnpscfname}  ${gnb_index}=0
    [Documentation]  This keyword is used to create SCF file base on package version
    ...
    ...  *AUTHOR* runrun.shou@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    |    =Input Parameters=     | =Man.= | =Description= |
    ...    | ne_type | Yes | product style, only support vcu, vdu |
    ...    | swversion | Yes | vdu software version like: vCUCNF00_0.300.13592 |
    ...    | pnpscfname   | Yes  | old scf file for pnp |
    ...    *RETURN VALUE*
    ...    scf plan name
    ${global_bts_id}  run keyword if  '${ne_type}' == 'vcu'  tl_config.get_cu_global_bts_id  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ...    ELSE  tl_config.get_du_global_bts_id  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ${pnp_scf_path}  tl_config.get_scf_yaml_filen_path  ne_type=${ne_type}  gnb_index=${gnb_index}
    ${pnp_scf_file}  Set Variable  ${pnp_scf_path}${pnpscfname}
    ${scffile}  netact_lcm.get_newversion_scf_pnp_part_file  swversion=${swversion}  oldscffile=${pnp_scf_file}
    ...    newscffilepath=${pnp_scf_path}
    ${scffilepart}  netact_lcm.rebuild_scf_file_for_pnp_part  scffilename=${scffile}  btsid=${global_bts_id}
    log to console  ${scffilepart}
    [Return]   ${scffilepart}


